<title>JAPAN: Group of Six officials to meet in Tokyo -- source.</title>
<headline>Group of Six officials to meet in Tokyo -- source.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senior finance ministry and central bank officials from five Asian economies -- Japan, China, Singapore, Australia and Hong Kong -- and the United States will meet in Tokyo on March 4, a financial source said on Monday.</p>
<p>A Japanese finance ministry official declined to comment on whether such a meeting would be held.</p>
<p>The financial source said the officials would discuss matters such as macroeconomic policies, financial market supervision and foreign exchange rates, as well as possible responses in the event of an Asian version of Mexico's financial crisis.</p>
</text>
